Package: parvenu
Title: Multithreaded Matching and Regex Detection for Large Vectors
Version: 0.0.0.9001
Authors@R: person("Lukas", "Jung", , "jung-lukas@gmx.net", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Multithreaded versions of match(), %in%, duplicated(),
    unique(), findInterval(), grepl(), regexpr(), sub(), and gsub(),
    written in Rust, and matching on several key columns at once. match(),
    %in%, duplicated(), unique(), and findInterval() give the same results
    as base R, and fall back to it below the size where threads pay off.
    Regex detection, counting, location, extraction, and replacement use
    the syntax of Rust's regex crate. Dictionary lookup finds which of many
    literal terms or regexes each string contains, how many hits it has, or
    replaces them all, in one pass per string.
